      <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="ch-now">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="section-label"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>Now</p>
          <h2 class="chapter-title" id="ch-now">Why this blog exists</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>I learned reverse engineering from other people's write-ups, so this is me returning the favor: deep dives done the old-fashioned way, experiments with AI in the loop, side projects, and the occasional opinion. If you're just getting started, you don't need much. Writing trainers for Flash games was enough for me back then, and a single-player game, Cheat Engine and Ghidra will get you just as far today.</p>
          <p>And if you're writing cheats right now and wondering whether those skills could ever pay for a legit career: <strong>they can</strong>. The industry hires people like us. I'm one of them. Switch while it's still easy to walk away. It only gets harder the deeper you're in.</p>
        </div>
